  <content>
  <section class="practice">

   <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Solve each system of equations to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson. Enter your answer as “(x,y)” in the space provided. If any coordinate is a non-integer, enter it in decimal format.</para>
<exercise id="_9bc99444-8aaa-47fe-a206-b69c41414c38" class="multiple-choice">
   <problem>
      <para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} –2x + 5y = –42\\ 7x + 2y = 30 \end{array}\right. \)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
      <para>\((0,15)\)</para>
      <para>\((11,−4)\)</para>
      <para>\((1,−8)\)</para>
      <para>\((6,−6)\)</para>
   </problem>
   <solution>
      <para>Correct! (6,−6)</para>
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.2. Revisit</para>
      <para>The correct answer is (6,−6).
    </para>
     <para>\(- 2( –2x+5y=–42)=4x-10y=84 \)
        \(5(7x+2y=30)=35x+10y=150\)
        \(5(7x+2y=30)=35x+10y=150\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{r}4x-10y&amp;=&amp;84
        \\35x+10y&amp;=&amp;150
        \\ \hline
        39x&amp;=&amp;234
        \\x&amp;=&amp;6
        \end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{r}4x-10y&amp;=&amp;84
        \\35x+10y&amp;=&amp;150
        \\ \hline
        39x&amp;=&amp;234
        \\x&amp;=&amp;6
        \end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}7x+8y&amp;=&amp;4
        \\7(6)+2y&amp;=&amp;30
        \\42+2y&amp;=&amp;30
        \\2y&amp;=&amp;-12
        \\y&amp;=&amp;-6
        \\\end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}7x+8y&amp;=&amp;4
        \\7(6)+2y&amp;=&amp;30
        \\42+2y&amp;=&amp;30
        \\2y&amp;=&amp;-12
        \\y&amp;=&amp;-6
        \\\end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((6,-6)\).</para>
      </solution>
   </exercise>
   <exercise id="_2d665fcc-760f-4664-95f6-6652b9a78b16" class="multiple-choice">
      <problem>
         <para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 6x – 5y = –34\\ 2x + 6y = 4 \end{array}\right. \)</para>
         <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
         <para>\((2,0)\)</para>
         <para>\((1,8)\)</para>
         <para>\((−4,2)\)</para>
         <para>\((−9,−4)\)</para>
      </problem>
      <solution>
         <para>Correct! (−4,2)</para>
         <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.2.</para>
     <para>The correct answer is (−4,2).</para>
     <para>\(- 3( 2x+6y=4)=-6x-18y=-12 \)</para>
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{r}6x–5y&amp;=&amp;34
        \\-6x-18y&amp;=&amp;12
        \\ \hline
        -23y&amp;=&amp;-46
        \\y&amp;=&amp;2
        \end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{r}6x–5y&amp;=&amp;34
        \\-6x-18y&amp;=&amp;12
        \\ \hline
        -23y&amp;=&amp;-46
        \\y&amp;=&amp;2
        \end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}7x+8y&amp;=&amp;4
        \\2x+6(2)&amp;=&amp;4
        \\2x+12&amp;=&amp;4
        \\2x&amp;=&amp;-8
        \\x&amp;=&amp;-4
        \\\end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}7x+8y&amp;=&amp;4
        \\2x+6(2)&amp;=&amp;4
        \\2x+12&amp;=&amp;4
        \\2x&amp;=&amp;-8
        \\x&amp;=&amp;-4
        \\\end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((-4,2)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((-4,2)\).</para>
     </solution>
   </exercise>

   <exercise id="_34358845-9f4c-49dd-9744-40f69306892c" class="multiple-choice">
      <problem>
         <para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 5x – y = –2.6\\ −4x − 6y = 1.4 \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((7,–4.9)\)</para><para>\((0.5,0.1)\)</para><para>\((−3,−12)\)</para><para>\((−0.5,0.1)\)</para>
      </problem>
         <solution>
            <para>Correct! (−0.5,0.1)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.2. Revisit</para>
            <para>The correct answer is (−0.5,0.1).</para>
            <para>\(- 6( 5x–y=–2.6)=-30x+6y=15.6 \)</para>
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{r}-30x+6y&amp;=&amp;15.6
        \\−4x−6y&amp;=&amp;1.4
        \\ \hline
        -34x&amp;=&amp;17
        \\x&amp;=&amp;-0.5
        \end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{r}-30x+6y&amp;=&amp;15.6
        \\−4x−6y&amp;=&amp;1.4
        \\ \hline
        -34x&amp;=&amp;17
        \\x&amp;=&amp;-0.5
        \end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}−4(-0.5)−6y&amp;=&amp;1.4
        \\2-6y&amp;=&amp;1.4
        \\-6y&amp;=&amp;-0.6
        \\y&amp;=&amp;0.1
        \\\end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}−4(-0.5)−6y&amp;=&amp;1.4
        \\2-6y&amp;=&amp;1.4
        \\-6y&amp;=&amp;-0.6
        \\y&amp;=&amp;0.1
        \\\end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((-0.5,0.1)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((-0.5,0.1)\).</para>
      </solution>
   </exercise>
   <exercise id="d5da2e2a-5854-4af4-9134-d43fb40d9570" class="multiple-choice">
      <problem><para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 7x – 2y = 3\\ 4x + 5y = 3.25 \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((1,2)\)</para><para>\((0.5,0.25)\)</para><para>\((–1,–5)\)</para><para>\((3,9)\)</para></problem>
      <solution><para>Correct! (0.5,0.25)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.2.</para>
     <para>The correct answer is (0.5,0.25).</para>
     <para>
      \(5( 7x–2y=3)=35x-10y=15 \)
        \(2(4x+5y=3.25)=8x+10y=6.5 \)
        \(2(4x+5y=3.25)=8x+10y=6.5 \)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{r}35x-10y&amp;=&amp;15
        \\8x+10y&amp;=&amp;6.5
        \\ \hline
        43x&amp;=&amp;21.5
        \\x&amp;=&amp;0.5
        \end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{r}35x-10y&amp;=&amp;15
        \\8x+10y&amp;=&amp;6.5
        \\ \hline
        43x&amp;=&amp;21.5
        \\x&amp;=&amp;0.5
        \end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}−4(0.5)+5y&amp;=&amp;3.25
        \\2+5y&amp;=&amp;3.25
        \\5y&amp;=&amp;1.25
        \\y&amp;=&amp;0.25
        \\\end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}−4(0.5)+5y&amp;=&amp;3.25
        \\2+5y&amp;=&amp;3.25
        \\5y&amp;=&amp;1.25
        \\y&amp;=&amp;0.25
        \\\end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((0.5,0.25)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((0.5,0.25)\).</para>
</solution>
</exercise>
<exercise id="_7d8cc503-792c-4f17-abd4-ca9cc3a74d71" class="multiple-choice">
   <problem><para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 5x + 9y = 16\\ x + 2y = 4 \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((−4,4)\)</para><para>\((3.2,0)\)</para><para>\((−8,6)\)</para><para>\((8,−2)\)</para></problem>
   <solution><para>Correct! (−4,4)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.3.</para>
      <para>The correct answer is (−4,4).</para>
      <para>\(5( 7x–2y=3)=35x-10y=15 \)</para>
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{r}5x+9y&amp;=&amp;16
        \\-5x-10y&amp;=&amp;-20
        \\ \hline
        -y&amp;=&amp;-4
        \\y&amp;=&amp;4
        \end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{r}5x+9y&amp;=&amp;16
        \\-5x-10y&amp;=&amp;-20
        \\ \hline
        -y&amp;=&amp;-4
        \\y&amp;=&amp;4
        \end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}x+2(4)&amp;=&amp;4
        \\x+8&amp;=&amp;4
        \\x&amp;=&amp;-4
        \\\end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}x+2(4)&amp;=&amp;4
        \\x+8&amp;=&amp;4
        \\x&amp;=&amp;-4
        \\\end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((-4,4)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((-4,4)\).</para>
    </para>
   </solution>
   </exercise>
   <exercise id="ffdacaf7-13f0-460e-8e9c-95b0d3445bd8" class="multiple-choice">
      <problem><para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} \frac{3}{2}x - \frac{1}{4}y = 5\\ \frac{1}{3}x + \frac{1}{6}y = 2 \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((4,4)\)</para><para>\((1,−5)\)</para><para>\((−\frac15,\frac23)\)</para><para>\((−4,−5)\)</para></problem>
      <solution>
         <para>Correct! \( (4,4) \)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \( (4,4) \).</para>
         <para>\( 4( \frac32 x-\frac14 y=5)=6x-y=20\)</para>
         <para>\(6( \frac13 x+\frac16 y=2)=2x+y=12\)</para>
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{array}{r} 6x-y&amp;=&amp;5
        \\ 2x+y&amp;=&amp;12
        \\ \hline
        8x&amp;=&amp;32
        \\x&amp;=&amp;4
        \end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{r} 6x-y&amp;=&amp;5
        \\ 2x+y&amp;=&amp;12
        \\ \hline
        8x&amp;=&amp;32
        \\x&amp;=&amp;4
        \end{array}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
      
 <para>
        \(\begin{align*}
        x + 2(4)y &amp;= 12 \\
        8 + y &amp;= 12 \\
        y &amp;= 4 \\
        \end{align*}\)
    </para>
     <para>The solution is \((4,4)\).</para>
   </solution>
</exercise>
<exercise id="acd91d7d-e4a8-45d6-b064-706857b5cc44" class="multiple-choice">
   <problem>
      <para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} \frac{1}{3}x + \frac{1}{9}y = 2\\ -\frac{1}{2}x + \frac{4}{5}y = -3 \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((6,0)\)</para><para>\((7,−3)\)</para><para>\((8,−5)\)</para><para>\((−2,−5)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! (6,0)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.3.</para>
         <para>The correct answer is (6,0).</para>
         <para>
            \(9( \frac13 x+ \frac19 y=2)=3x+y=18 \)
        \(10( –\frac12 x+ \frac45 y=–3)=-5x+8y=-30 \)
        \(10( –\frac12 x+ \frac45 y=–3)=-5x+8y=-30 \)
        \(-8( 3x+y=18)=-24x-8y=-144 \)
        \(-8( 3x+y=18)=-24x-8y=-144 \)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{align*}-5x+8y&amp;=-30
        \\-24x-8y&amp;=-144
        \\ \hline
        -29x&amp;=-174
        \\x&amp;=6
        \\\end{align*}\)
        \(\begin{align*}-5x+8y&amp;=-30
        \\-24x-8y&amp;=-144
        \\ \hline
        -29x&amp;=-174
        \\x&amp;=6
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
      <para>
        \(\begin{align*}3x+y&amp;=18
        \\(3(6)+y&amp;=18
        \\18+y&amp;=18
        \\y&amp;=0
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
      <para>
        \(\begin{align*}3x+y&amp;=18
        \\(3(6)+y&amp;=18
        \\18+y&amp;=18
        \\y&amp;=0
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((6,0)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((6,0)\).</para>
</solution>
</exercise>
<exercise id="_786245a2-01a9-446a-9503-4d7bea9acdba" class="multiple-choice">
   <problem><para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 6x - 8y = \frac{16}{5}\\ 3x + 2y = \frac{14}{5} \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((4,−4.6)\)</para><para>\((0,−0.4)\)</para><para>\((0.8,0.2)\)</para><para>\((2,1.1)\)</para></problem>
   <solution><para>Correct! (0.8,0.2)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.2.</para>
      <para>The correct answer is (0.8,0.2).</para><para>\( 4( 3x+2y=\frac{14}{5})=12x+8y=\frac{56}{5} \)</para>
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{align*}6x-8y&amp;=\frac{16}{5}
        \\12x+8y&amp;=\frac{56}{5}
        \\ \hline
        18x&amp;=\frac{72}{5}
        \\90x&amp;=72
        \\x&amp;=\frac{72}{90}
        \\x&amp;=\frac{4}{5}
        \\x&amp;=0.8
        \\\end{align*}\)
        \(\begin{align*}6x-8y&amp;=\frac{16}{5}
        \\12x+8y&amp;=\frac{56}{5}
        \\ \hline
        18x&amp;=\frac{72}{5}
        \\90x&amp;=72
        \\x&amp;=\frac{72}{90}
        \\x&amp;=\frac{4}{5}
        \\x&amp;=0.8
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
<para>
        \(\begin{align*}3(\frac45)+2y&amp;=\frac{14}{5}
        \\\frac{12}{5}+2y&amp;=\frac{14}{5}
        \\5(\frac{12}{5}+2y&amp;=\frac{14}{5})
        \\12+10y&amp;=14
        \\10y&amp;=2
        \\y&amp;=\frac{2}{10}
        \\y&amp;=\frac15
        \\y&amp;=0.2
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
      <para>
        \(\begin{align*}3(\frac45)+2y&amp;=\frac{14}{5}
        \\\frac{12}{5}+2y&amp;=\frac{14}{5}
        \\5(\frac{12}{5}+2y&amp;=\frac{14}{5})
        \\12+10y&amp;=14
        \\10y&amp;=2
        \\y&amp;=\frac{2}{10}
        \\y&amp;=\frac15
        \\y&amp;=0.2
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((0.8,0.2)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((0.8,0.2)\).</para>
  </solution>
</exercise>
<exercise id="b2357ec1-f9da-4c47-98f6-69f02e394cc1" class="multiple-choice">
   <problem><para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 5x – 2y = 2 \\ 7x – 4y = 2.5 \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2.4,5)\)</para><para>\((2,4)\)</para><para>\((0,−1)\)</para><para>\((0.5,0.25)\)</para></problem>
   <solution>
      <para>Correct! (0.5,0.25)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.2.</para>
      <para>The correct answer is (0.5,0.25).</para>
      <para>\(-2(5x-2y=2)=-10x+4y=-4\)</para>
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{align*}-10x+4y&amp;=-4
        \\7x-4y&amp;=2.5
        \\ \hline
        -3x&amp;=-1.5
        \\x&amp;=0.5
        \end{align*}\)
        \(\begin{align*}-10x+4y&amp;=-4
        \\7x-4y&amp;=2.5
        \\ \hline
        -3x&amp;=-1.5
        \\x&amp;=0.5
        \end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
<para>
        \(\begin{align*}5(0.5)-2y&amp;=2
        \\2.5-2y&amp;=2
        \\-2y&amp;=-0.5
        \\y&amp;=0.25
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
      <para>
        \(\begin{align*}5(0.5)-2y&amp;=2
        \\2.5-2y&amp;=2
        \\-2y&amp;=-0.5
        \\y&amp;=0.25
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((0.5,0.25)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((0.5,0.25)\).</para>
   </solution>
</exercise>
<exercise id="_326adc26-1990-4c2e-93b2-252ca0784e1d" class="multiple-choice">
   <problem><para>\( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} \frac{1}{2}x + \frac{1}{3}y = \frac{1}{3}\\ \frac{1}{3}x + \frac{1}{4}y = -\frac{1}{8} \end{array}\right. \)</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((9,–12.5)\)</para><para>\((0,1)\)</para><para>\((6,–8)\)</para><para>\((12,–17)\)</para></problem>
   <solution><para>Correct! (9,–12.5)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.6.3.
    </para><para>The correct answer is (9,–12.5).</para>
     <para>
      \(6( \frac12 x+\frac13 y=\frac13)=3x+2y=2 \)
        \(24( \frac13 x+\frac14 y=–\frac18)=8x+6y=-3 \)
        \(24( \frac13 x+\frac14 y=–\frac18)=8x+6y=-3 \)
        \(-3(3x+2y=2)=-9x-6y=-6\)
        \(-3(3x+2y=2)=-9x-6y=-6\)
     </para>  
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <para>
        \(\begin{align*}-9x-6y&amp;=-6
        \\8x+6y&amp;=-3
        \\ \hline
        -x&amp;=-9
        \\x&amp;=9
        \\\end{align*}\)
        \(\begin{align*}-9x-6y&amp;=-6
        \\8x+6y&amp;=-3
        \\ \hline
        -x&amp;=-9
        \\x&amp;=9
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
<para>
        \(\begin{align*}3(9)+2y&amp;=2
        \\27+2y&amp;=2
        \\2y&amp;=-25
        \\y=&amp;-12.5
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
      <para>
        \(\begin{align*}3(9)+2y&amp;=2
        \\27+2y&amp;=2
        \\2y&amp;=-25
        \\y=&amp;-12.5
        \\\end{align*}\)
     </para>
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        <para>The solution is \((9,-12.5)\).</para>
      
        <para>The solution is \((9,-12.5)\).</para>
      </solution>
   </exercise>
</section>
</content>
